<section class="section section--tight">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="note disclaimer-note"><strong>Partner terms are not open for sign-up.</strong> This page sets out the rules that come first. For your own professional obligations, rely on your institute's published guidance.</div>
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2>What to check before working with any business that brings you clients</h2>
      <p>This applies to any platform or business that sends you work, not only ours. Rules differ by profession, so the answer for a bookkeeper may not hold for a CA or an advocate.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="data-table-wrap" tabindex="0" aria-label="Professional rules, scrolls sideways on small screens">
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">If you are</th><th scope="col">What we have read</th><th scope="col">Questions to take to your adviser or body</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">A Chartered Accountant in practice</th>
            <td>ICAI's Code of Ethics, 13th edition: members and firms may not list with online application-based aggregators "for services which are exclusively reserved for Chartered Accountants", with "no restriction on listing for non-exclusive Services". The First Schedule also addresses commission to non-members, securing work through non-employees, and solicitation.</td>
            <td>Does this platform count as an aggregator? Is an introduction a listing? Does any payment fall within the commission rule? ICAI encourages use of its own portal, {% ext "https://caconnect.icai.org/", "CA Connect" %}.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">An advocate</th>
            <td>Bar Council of India Rule 36 restricts soliciting and advertising, directly or indirectly. Press reports describe 2024 and 2025 action by the Bar Council concerning online portals, with related appeals reported before the Supreme Court.</td>
            <td>Can you take part at all? We have not read the orders ourselves, and the position may have moved.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">A GST practitioner, tax practitioner, cost accountant or company secretary</th>
            <td>We have not completed a review of the rules that apply to you.</td>
            <td>Check with your own professional body or the relevant authority.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">An accountant or bookkeeper without those titles</th>
            <td>We have not identified a professional body rule, but have not reviewed this fully.</td>
            <td>Which of your services are reserved for others? Do not take on or describe reserved work.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>
    <p class="section-foot">Bar Council and other rules may change. Quoted ICAI wording: {% ext "https://resource.cdn.icai.org/92475coe2026v1.pdf", "Code of Ethics, 13th edition, Volume I" %}, clause 3.5, page 157; First Schedule Part I, clauses (2), (5) and (6). Read the source itself, because other provisions may apply.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="would-title">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <h2 id="would-title">What partner terms would need to cover</h2>
      <ul class="tick-list plain-list">
        <li>A qualified review of how these rules apply</li>
        <li>Whether, and how, any professional would pay AccountOrbit</li>
        <li>How enquiries would be routed and shared</li>
        <li>What checks would be made, and how they would be described</li>
        <li>A written agreement</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="para">Partner terms are not open for sign-up. If you would like to discuss them, call <a href="{{ site.phoneHref }}">{{ site.phoneDisplay }}</a>.</p>
      {% gap "any partner terms." %}
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>What we would never say about you</h2>
      <ul class="tick-list tick-list--no plain-list">
        <li>That you are "our accountant" or part of AccountOrbit</li>
        <li>That you have been verified, unless a real check was done</li>
        <li>Ratings, results or fees that you have not supplied and evidenced</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
